From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:39:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: google,gs201-decon: Add the Tensor G3

The Tensor G3 (zuma) DECON0 is the Tensor G4's: Google's display driver
builds zuma with the same CAL (cal_9865), and the Pixel 8 Pro's stock
DECON0 node has zumapro's main registers (0x19470000), DPP0 read DMA
(0x19900000), interrupts (SPI 243, 242, 241) and fourteen windows. Add
its compatible.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
---
 .../bindings/display/samsung/google,gs201-decon.yaml       | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/samsung/google,gs201-decon.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/samsung/google,gs201-decon.yaml
index 58709681c..baf0a8b90 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/samsung/google,gs201-decon.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/samsung/google,gs201-decon.yaml
@@ -10,9 +10,9 @@ maintainers:
   - Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
 
 description:
-  The DECON is the display controller of the gs201 (Tensor G2) and zumapro
-  (Tensor G4) display pipelines. It blends up to six or fourteen windows,
-  respectively, each fed by a DPP read DMA
+  The DECON is the display controller of the gs201 (Tensor G2), zuma
+  (Tensor G3) and zumapro (Tensor G4) display pipelines. It blends up to
+  six (gs201) or fourteen windows, each fed by a DPP read DMA
   channel, compresses the result with DSC and hands it to a DSIM. In
   command mode a frame is sent on each tearing effect (TE) pulse of the
   panel; register writes are double-buffered and take effect at the
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@ properties:
   compatible:
     enum:
       - google,gs201-decon
+      - google,zuma-decon
       - google,zumapro-decon
 
   reg:
